      "content": "Those repeated service fees and unexplained transaction declines are common tactics used by credit unions to discourage members from holding large balances or switching providers. While fraud and account monitoring can sometimes cause such issues, consistent financial difficulty is often a method to pressure loyalty members into leaving. I strongly recommend contacting your union immediately to dispute these charges and request a review of your account status with your Supervisory Officer.",
